  "verbalization": "Dexamethasone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Stevens-Johnson Syndrome (SJS) through a chain of indications that link it to Triamcinolone, a corticosteroid with known immunosuppressive properties. The evidence suggests that Dexamethasone, when used in conjunction with other conditions like Chronic Beryllium Disease or Erythema Multiforme, may contribute to the development of SJS via an indirect mechanism involving Triamcinolone. This connection is supported by the shared pathway of indication from Dexamethasone to Triamcinolone, followed by a common indication to SJS, implying a potential role of Triamcinolone in the inflammatory or immunological processes underlying SJS. The overlapping pathways highlight a possible mechanistic link between corticosteroids and SJS, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
